frontier/campaigns/2026-10-26/new-discoveries/lanes/pi-euler-turan-final-review/fresh/trureturing/Blueprint/D5/S3/Combinatorics/Sequenceability/PairedQuantitativeOrdering.md [[23, 'This improves understanding of event overlap where the first-moment estimate fails. The corresponding words are known as rooted connected chord diagrams after forgetting coordinate names and signs. Mahmoud and Yeats, Connected Chord Diagrams and the Combinatorics of Asymptotic Expansions, arXiv:2010.06550v2, give a stronger asymptotic expansion for that established class. No novelty or priority for this finite certificate is claimed. This result concerns this paired alphabet only; unrestricted AM and arbitrary-subset sequenceability are not resolved.\n']]
